flf2a$ 4 2 7 -1 36 0 0 557

MS-DOS FIGfont (phm-dos.flf) by Philippe Majerus (www.phm.lu)
This font uses Unicode 16.0 octant characters to render characters based on
the original MS-DOS 6.22 EGA/2/3.CPI fonts for 80 columns × 25 lines mode.

Unified in this FIGfont are the characters from the following codepages:
- 437 (OEM - United States)
- 737 (OEM - Greek 437G) - using 869 Modern Greek glyphs
- 775 (OEM - Baltic) - not supported by MS-DOS
- 850 (OEM - Multilingual Latin I) and ISO 8859-1 (Latin 1)
- 852 (OEM - Latin II)
- 855 (OEM - Cyrillic)
- 857 (OEM - Turkish)
- 858 (OEM - Multilingual Latin I + Euro)
- 860 (OEM - Portuguese)
- 861 (OEM - Icelandic)
- 862 (OEM - Hebrew) - from Hebrew Support for MS-DOS version 1.0
- 863 (OEM - Canadian French)
- 865 (OEM - Nordic)
- 866 (OEM - Russian)
- 869 (OEM - Modern Greek)
- 1250 (ANSI - Central Europe)
- 1251 (ANSI - Cyrillic)
- 1252 (ANSI - Latin I)
- 1253 (ANSI - Greek)
- 1254 (ANSI - Turkish)
- 1257 (ANSI - Baltic)

Note the MS-DOS CPI fonts for 80×25 text mode are really 9×16 characters in
a 720×400 screen, but the glyphs are 8×16 with a 9th column that is either
padding, or a repeat of the 8th one for box drawing characters to touch.
This font contains them as 8×16 to fit within octants, which means it cannot
include the extra 1px spacing available in the original.

Date: February 26 - May 3, 2026

